  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During the 33rd APEC Summit held in China, President Prabowo Subianto led the Indonesian delegation, accompanied by Bahlil Lahadalia, the Coordinating Minister for Downstream and Energy Transition, who focused on advancing national energy diplomacy. Throughout the summit, the president addressed the necessity of global leadership from major powers, specifically referencing the meeting between heads of state from the United States, Russia, and China. Prabowo underscored the importance of digital economic growth and food security while cautioning that technological advancements and AI must be managed to reduce global inequality. Discussions also touched upon nuclear policy and international peace. The Indonesian government indicated that engagement during this multilateral event resulted in significant investment commitments for the country, estimated to reach approximately Rp 1,600 trillion as part of ongoing efforts to foster regional and global economic cooperation.",
